00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,111
Food Safety: A Shared Responsibility, A Business Imperative.

2
00:00:05,061 --> 00:00:15,163
Editorial Food Safety: A Shared Responsibility, A Business Imperative Dear Readers, India’s food sector is at an important point in its growth journey.

3
00:00:15,163 --> 00:00:25,788
As food processing, organised retail, food services and digital commerce expand, consumers are becoming increasingly conscious of quality, safety and provenance.

4
00:00:25,788 --> 00:00:35,254
Food safety is therefore no longer merely a regulatory requirement; it is fundamental to consumer confidence, competitiveness and sustainable growth.

5
00:00:35,254 --> 00:00:37,595
The scale is significant.

6
00:00:37,595 --> 00:00:45,413
FSSAI data indicates that India has more than 50 lakh registered food businesses and over 25 lakh licences.

7
00:00:45,413 --> 00:00:56,493
In 2025–26, more than 3 lakh inspections were conducted and around 3 lakh food samples tested, while over 30 lakh food handlers received training.

8
00:00:56,493 --> 00:01:03,356
These numbers underline the scale of the ecosystem and the need to embed safety across the entire value chain.

9
00:01:03,356 --> 00:01:14,743
For industry, the focus must increasingly shift from reactive compliance to prevention—from raw-material sourcing and processing to packaging, storage, transportation and consumption.

10
00:01:14,743 --> 00:01:22,402
Traceability, testing, cold-chain Prashant infrastructure, quality systems and trained people must work together.

11
00:01:22,402 --> 00:01:34,049
Technology can strengthen this approach Girbane through IoT-enabled monitoring, digital traceability and AI-led analysis, making food-safety systems more responsive and preventive.

12
00:01:34,049 --> 00:01:41,459
At MCCIA, this responsibility is reflected in our work across the food and agriculture ecosystem.

13
00:01:41,459 --> 00:01:54,629
The Food Processing Committee, chaired by Retired IAS Umesh Chandra Sarangi, has been undertaking important initiatives to strengthen the sector and create greater connect between industry, technology and policy.

14
00:01:54,629 --> 00:02:15,720
The Agriculture Export Facilitation Centre (AEFC) recently conducted a five-day Agri-Food EXIM Management Certification Course in August 2026, equipping participants with practical knowledge across product selection, market identification, compliance, buyer discovery, export pricing, payments and international logistics.

15
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:26,140
Our MSME Helpline also provides consultations to enterprises in the agriculture and food-processing sectors, helping businesses navigate practical challenges.

16
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:31,947
Food safety is also closely linked to infrastructure and the wider business environment.

17
00:02:31,947 --> 00:02:49,913
A recent MCCIA interaction with the Pune Metropolitan Region Development Authority (PMRDA), brought industry concerns from Pirangut–Urawade and Chakan to the table, including development permissions, road alignment, traffic, waste management, drainage and environmental issues.

18
00:02:49,913 --> 00:03:01,924
PMRDA officials assured monthly review meetings and time-bound action on several company-specific cases, reinforcing the importance of responsive infrastructure and governance for industrial growth.

19
00:03:01,924 --> 00:03:05,447
Ultimately, food safety is about trust.

20
00:03:05,447 --> 00:03:12,447
It requires collaboration among industry, government, technology providers and knowledge institutions.

21
00:03:12,447 --> 00:03:22,163
This special issue of Sampada brings together perspectives on regulation, technology, quality systems and the practical challenges shaping the food value chain.

22
00:03:22,163 --> 00:03:34,834
At MCCIA, we believe that building safety into everyday business practices will not only protect consumers but also make India’s food ecosystem more competitive, resilient and globally ready.

23
00:03:34,834 --> 00:03:38,311
Food safety is everyone’s responsibility.

24
00:03:38,311 --> 00:03:43,049
Making it an integral part of business is the opportunity before us.

25
00:03:43,049 --> 00:03:58,243
